---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import MessageDemo from "../../components/MessageDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Message"
  description="Chat messages with bubbles in seven fills, reactions, avatars, names, and reply status."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Message</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Lays out one chat message: an avatar beside a column of bubbles, cards, and
    actions, with a small name line above and a status line below. Bubbles come
    in seven fills and can carry a pill of reactions.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><MessageDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Message usage"
      code={`import {
  Message,
  MessageAvatar,
  MessageBubble,
  MessageContent,
  MessageFooter,
  MessageGroup,
  MessageHeader,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/message";

<MessageGroup>
  <Message align="start">
    <MessageAvatar>
      <Avatar><AvatarFallback>AM</AvatarFallback></Avatar>
    </MessageAvatar>
    <MessageContent>
      <MessageHeader>Alex Meadow · 10:30</MessageHeader>
      <MessageBubble variant="secondary">Can you help plan the garden?</MessageBubble>
      <MessageFooter>Delivered</MessageFooter>
    </MessageContent>
  </Message>
  <Message align="end">
    <MessageContent>
      <MessageBubble>Yes. Let's start with the planting list.</MessageBubble>
      <MessageBubble>Tomatoes and basil go in the south bed.</MessageBubble>
    </MessageContent>
  </Message>
</MessageGroup>`}
    />
    <p>
      Put bubbles, text, cards, or buttons inside <code>MessageContent</code>.
      Consecutive bubbles from one sender go in the same
      <code>MessageContent</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>align</code> is <code>"start"</code>, the default, or <code
        >"end"</code
      >. An end message puts the avatar on the trailing side and moves every
      direct child of <code>MessageContent</code> that has a <code
        >data-slot</code
      > to the end. A child without a slot, such as a plain <code>div</code>,
      keeps its own width. The footer text also moves to the end. There are no
      sizes: text is 14px, the header and footer are 12px.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>MessageGroup</code> stacks messages 8px apart. Inside a message, the avatar
      and content are 8px apart and the content's children are 10px apart. <code
        >MessageAvatar</code
      > is at least 32px wide and sits at the bottom of the message. When the content
      ends with a <code>MessageFooter</code>, the avatar moves up so it sits
      beside the last bubble.
    </p>
    <p>
      The header and footer are inset 12px so they line up with padded bubble
      text. When a direct child of the content has <code
        >data-variant="ghost"</code
      >, a bubble without padding, the inset drops to 0.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every part takes the props of a <code>div</code>, including <code
        >ref</code
      >, so you can read the rendered bubbles from <code>MessageContent</code>
      for copy actions.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Bubbles</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Bubble variants"
      code={`<Message align="end">
  <MessageContent>
    <MessageBubble variant="secondary">
      Create a Customers table with Name, Email, Company, Phone, and Status.
    </MessageBubble>
  </MessageContent>
</Message>

<Message>
  <MessageContent>
    <MessageBubble variant="ghost">{answer}</MessageBubble>
  </MessageContent>
</Message>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>MessageBubble</code> is at most 80% of its column and as wide as its text.
      There is one size: 14px text with 8px by 12px padding and the panel radius.
      A bubble has no side of its own. It moves to the end inside
      <code>Message align="end"</code>, or inside any element with
      <code>data-slot="message"</code> and <code>data-align="end"</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>variant</code> sets the fill. <code>"default"</code> uses the primary
      color for your own messages. <code>"secondary"</code> is for prompts sent to
      an agent. <code>"muted"</code> is a lighter fill for quiet notes. <code
        >"tinted"</code
      > mixes in the primary color so it follows a brand theme. <code
        >"outline"</code
      > draws a border for quoted text.
      <code>"ghost"</code> drops the fill and padding and may span the full width,
      for agent answers. <code>"destructive"</code> marks a message that failed.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Reactions</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="A reaction pill"
      code={`import { MessageBubble, MessageReactions } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/message";

<MessageBubble
  variant="secondary"
  reactions={<MessageReactions align="start" side="bottom">🌱 2</MessageReactions>}
>
  Hello from Alex.
</MessageBubble>`}
    />
    <p>
      Pass a <code>MessageReactions</code> to the <code>reactions</code> prop. It
      pins a pill over the <code>"top"</code> or <code>"bottom"</code> edge, 12px
      in from the <code>"start"</code> or <code>"end"</code> corner. The defaults
      are <code>side="bottom"</code> and <code>align="end"</code>. With
      reactions, the bubble and pill are wrapped in an element with
      <code>data-slot="message-bubble-frame"</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Leave room around a bubble with reactions. The pill hangs three quarters
      outside it. Its 3px ring uses <code>--sprout-message-reactions-ring</code
      >, which defaults to the surface color. Set it to the background behind
      the bubble.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Links and buttons</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Interactive bubbles"
      code={`<MessageBubble variant="outline" render={<a href="/results/investor-update" />}>
  Open result · Investor update draft
</MessageBubble>

<Message align="end">
  <MessageContent>
    <MessageBubble
      variant="destructive"
      render={<button type="button" />}
      onClick={retry}
    >
      Couldn't send. Retry
    </MessageBubble>
  </MessageContent>
</Message>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>render</code> swaps the bubble element. A link or button keeps the variant
      fill, gets a slightly stronger fill on hover, and shows a focus ring when reached
      with the keyboard. Reactions sit outside the bubble element, so a bubble rendered
      as a button can still hold reaction buttons. Buttons inside <code
        >MessageReactions</code
      > become 24px toggles. Set <code>aria-pressed</code> and an <code
        >aria-label</code
      > with the count.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every bubble has <code>data-slot="message-bubble"</code>, so a copy action
      can collect the text of each bubble in a message.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Reply status</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Failed reply footer"
      code={`<Message align="end">
  <MessageContent>
    <MessageBubble variant="secondary">{text}</MessageBubble>
    <MessageFooter>
      <p role="status"><Danger aria-hidden="true" /> The reply didn't finish.</p>
      <Button size="sm" variant="outline" onClick={retry}>Retry reply</Button>
    </MessageFooter>
  </MessageContent>
</Message>

<Message align="start" aria-busy="true">
  <MessageContent>
    <span className="sr-only">TulipFarm said</span>
    {streamedText}
  </MessageContent>
</Message>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Message and its bubbles add no role and are not focusable. Put messages in
      a list or a labelled region and let links, buttons, and bubbles rendered
      as either take focus in reading order. Make a scrolling conversation a
      focusable, labelled region so it can be scrolled with the keyboard. When a
      reply has no visible name, add visually hidden text such as "TulipFarm
      said". Mark a reply that is still streaming with <code>aria-busy</code>,
      and announce status changes with <code>role="status"</code> or <code
        >role="alert"</code
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      Colors and fills change in 120ms and stop when reduced motion is
      requested. In forced colors mode every filled bubble and reaction pill
      gets a border. The layout uses logical sides, so end messages flip in
      right-to-left text.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The header and footer use <code>--sprout-muted</code>. The avatar slot
      uses <code>--sprout-secondary</code> behind images that do not fill it. Text
      uses <code>--sprout-text</code>, <code>--sprout-text-sm</code>, and
      <code>--sprout-text-xs</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Bubble fills use <code>--sprout-primary</code>,
      <code>--sprout-secondary</code>, <code>--sprout-surface</code>,
      <code>--sprout-line</code>, and <code>--sprout-danger-subtle</code>.
      Radius follows <code>--sprout-radius-panel</code>. The reaction ring uses
      <code>--sprout-message-reactions-ring</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
